<title>USA: Goodrich Petroleum Corp Q1 net increases.</title>
<headline>Goodrich Petroleum Corp Q1 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>For the three months ended</p>
<p>						    March 31,</p>
<p>				  (Pro Forma*)</p>
<p>					  1997	  1997	  1996</p>
<p> Revenues			 4,118,525 $ 3,597,419   2,650,788</p>
<p> Net Income			 971,443     736,958     276,365</p>
<p> Preferred Stock Dividends    314,878     263,315     162,230</p>
<p>Earnings Applicable to</p>
<p>   Common Stock		   656,565     473,643     114,135</p>
<p>Earnings per Average</p>
<p>   Common Share			 .02	   .01	   ---</p>
<p>Net Cash Flows From Operations</p>
<p>Before Working Capital Changes</p>
<p>				    2,325,787   1,945,947   1,458,883</p>
<p>Common Shares Outstanding</p>
<p>				   41,804,510  41,804,510  41,804,510</p>
<p>NOTE:  Net income was calculated before the payment of preferred dividends, earnings per share were calculated after the payment of preferred dividends.</p>
<p>The Company also released first quarter 1997 financial results on a pro forma basis as if the January 1997 acquisition of La/Cal Energy Partners II and related properties had been completed January 1, 1997.  The company did say, however, that the pro forma financial information is not necessarily indicative of the results it would have achieved had such transactions actually occurred on the date assumed.</p>
</text>
